-- lib/emitu.cub — the C printer with words, pairs and flat data unboxed (plan 18.7, B16 milestone 2:
-- types on the first-order form). Loaded after lib/emitc.cub (its runtime and byte strings). A type
-- here is W (uint64_t) or P (a boxed V *, as lib/emitc.cub prints everything); every local,
-- parameter and return is typed by inference — a parameter by its uses in the body (arithmetic W,
-- a switch's scrutinee or a buffer P, an argument of a call by that call's parameter), a return by
-- its body — and a value is converted where the inferred and the wanted types differ (mkw, ->n).
-- A loop whose body is the shape lower-welim makes (if c then continue (state) else break r) is
-- printed as a for loop over typed state variables with no allocation; other loops, closures and
-- constructors keep the boxed protocol. emit-prog-u defs: the program, main printing f_0's value.
